{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And Rebecca had a brother, and his name was Laban, etc.</b> According to our Rabbis of blessed memory (Numbers Rabbah 10; Esther Rabbah 6:3), who said that the righteous — their name precedes them, as it is written (Ruth 2:1) ״וּשְׁמוֹ בּוֹעַז״, ״וְשֵׁם הָאִישׁ אֱלִימֶלֶךְ״ (Ruth 1:2) — but the wicked, they precede their name, as it is written (I Samuel 25:25) ״נָבָל שְׁמוֹ״, etc. If so, why did the verse adopt the order of the righteous for Laban the wicked? And to give a reason for the matter, there is a fine point to raise in the verse's saying <b>וַיָּרָץ</b> — why did he run? And our Rabbis of blessed memory (Yalkut Shimoni 109) said: because he saw the nose-ring, etc., he set his eyes on the money. Yet it is still difficult: if so, it should have first said ״וַיְהִי כִּרְאוֹת״, etc., ״וַיָּרָץ״, etc. Also in this, why was it necessary to write twice ״אֶל הָאִישׁ הַחוּצָה אֶל הָעָיִן״?" "<b>Indeed</b>, the intention is that this man Laban hurried to meet the man knowing what had passed between him and Rebecca from the matters and from the closeness of knowledge, and he is a foreign man — this tells that there are things within. Therefore he donned zeal and ran to meet him to confront him with his zeal for his sister's zeal. And from the aspect of this deed, HaShem attributes him with the attribution of the righteous and said <b>וּשְׁמוֹ לָבָן</b>, for he performed a deed of the righteous in this, and the Holy One, blessed be He, does not withhold the reward of any creature." "And its saying <b>וַיְהִי כִּרְאוֹת</b>, etc., tells that what preceded was before seeing the bracelets and before hearing his sister's words. The order of events: his suspicion of Eliezer concerning an ugly matter, but once he saw the nose-ring, etc., and once he heard, etc., ״כָּכָה דִּבֶּר אֵלַי הָאִישׁ״ — his anger subsided. And even so, the verse informs that he went out to meet the man not to do harm, but on the contrary, to host him and to show him kindness, and with this it is resolved."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:16.885333259Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}